<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Smidt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1773">1773</a>–<a href="/years/1857">1857</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Smidt was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> theologian and statesman who served many terms as the city's mayor between 1821 and 1857. He represented Bremen at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>, helping to secure its independence as a free city in the German Confederation. In 1827 he bought land at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremerhaven">Bremerhaven</a> as the city's seaport.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-smidt.jpg" alt="Johann Smidt" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelmine Suhrlandt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SuhrlandtWSmidt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
